      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the total distance Ryosuke drove his friend that day, the gas used for that distance, and the cost of the gas.\n\nFirst, we calculate the distance driven:\n\\[ 74,592 - 74,568 = 24 \\text{ miles} \\]\n\nNext, we determine the amount of gas used:\nSince Ryosuke's car gets 28 miles per gallon, we divide the distance by the car's mileage:\n\\[ \\frac{24 \\text{ miles}}{28 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = \\frac{24}{28} = \\frac{6}{7} \\text{ gallons} \\]\n\nNow, we calculate the cost of the gas:\nThe price of one gallon of gas is $4.05, so the cost of \\(\\frac{6}{7}\\) gallons is:\n\\[ \\frac{6}{7} \\times 4.05 \\]\n\nTo perform the multiplication, we first convert \\(4.05\\) into a fraction:\n\\[ 4.05 = \\frac{405}{100} = \\frac{81}{20} \\]\n\nSo the cost becomes:\n\\[ \\frac{6}{7} \\times \\frac{81}{20} \\]\n\nTo multiply these fractions, we multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:\n\\[ \\frac{6 \\times 81}{7 \\times 20} = \\frac{486}{140} \\]\n\nNow we simplify \\(\\frac{486}{140}\\):\n\\[ \\frac{486}{140} = \\frac{243}{70} \\]\n\nNext, we convert \\(\\frac{243}{70}\\) to a decimal:\n\\[ \\frac{243}{70} \\approx 3.4714 \\]\n\nFinally, we round to the nearest cent:\n\\[ 3.4714 \\approx 3.47 \\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of the gas used to drive his friend back home from work is:\n\\[ \\boxed{3.47} \\]",
